query:
For \eqref{eq:Vprime_model}, show that in the one-cut ansatz \eqref{eq:onecut_ansatz} it is consistent to take
\begin{equation}\label{eq:Mpoly_form}
M(z)=g z^2 + p z + q,
\end{equation}
with constants $p,q$ (depending on $g,h,a,b$).

Now set $h=0$ but keep $g>0$ in \eqref{eq:Vprime_model}, so $V'(z)=z+gz^3$ is even.
Assume the one-cut support is symmetric: $a=-A$, $b=+A$ with $A>0$.
Using \eqref{eq:onecut_ansatz} with \eqref{eq:Mpoly_form} and the asymptotic \eqref{eq:asymptotic},
derive:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:A2_result}
A^2=\frac{\sqrt{1+8g}-1}{g},
\end{equation}
and the planar density
\begin{equation}\label{eq:rho_quartic_even}
\rho_0(x)=\frac{1}{2\pi}\left(gx^2+q_0\right)\sqrt{A^2-x^2}\;\mathbf{1}_{|x|\le A},
\qquad
q_0=\frac{4}{A^2}.
\end{equation}
